    "020": "The inbound garnishment order supplies the attachable-portion calculation inputs that the payroll engine must map: the order identifies the debt type and creditor, and the engine must apply the Judicial Code Art. 1409 net-wage bands to determine the attachable portion and compute the correct withholding amount. This is a genuine product touchpoint — the Art. 1409 band calculation cannot be performed without the order being mapped into the engine, and it feeds the matching outbound leg BE-OUT-GARNISHMENT to the bailiff or creditor. Contrast with LIMOSA and work-accident-insurer entries, which are filed entirely outside the payroll engine and therefore require no product mapping.",
